# Build output — regenerated by build.py, published by the Action as a Pages artifact.
# Not committed: the deployed site is always a product of data + templates (C-34).
_site/

# Font sources. The full upstream files are build inputs, not shipped artifacts.
# The SUBSET woff2 files under assets/fonts/ ARE committed — they are self-hosted (C-04).
build/fonts-src/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Node tooling (Lighthouse CI / axe, wired in P3.5)
node_modules/
.lighthouseci/

# OS
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Logs
*.log

# CI-written measurement output.
#
# data/generated/audit.json is IGNORED BUT COMMITTED, deliberately, and the two
# facts have to be read together. It is ignored so that a local build never
# accidentally commits locally-measured numbers over CI's — the builder has no
# browser and no published origin, so any figure produced here is exactly what
# the standing principle says is not evidence. It is then force-added by the
# ONE workflow allowed to write it (.github/workflows/measure-live.yml, via
# `git add -f`), because /audit renders from the committed file: if it were
# genuinely absent from the repository, every measured cell would read
# "— AT DEPLOY" on every deploy.
#
# The earlier comment here said only "Deliberately NOT committed", which stopped
# being true when D-42 made measure-live.yml the single writer. Corrected as
# finding 9b of the post-release deviation audit.
data/generated/audit.json

# Intermediate tool output, genuinely never committed. These exist only inside
# a CI run. They are listed so the scheduled jobs' single-path guard — which
# fails on ANY unexpected working-tree change — does not trip over the tooling's
# own by-products.
vnu.json
axe.json
gates.json
.lighthouseci/
